## Non-Mermaid description (accessible alternative)

Development splits contain only pilot task templates and injectors. The
confirmatory evaluation withholds entire task templates, new injector
implementations, entire fault families, and new fault compositions, and
adds an external L4 arm of naturally occurring failures. Fault-family
attribution on the unseen-family split is forced to "unknown" rather than
guessed. The primary H1/H2 analysis uses the unseen-task, unseen-injector,
and unseen-composition splits.
